<title>UK: Landesgirokasse plans $500 mln 5-yr bond.</title>
<headline>Landesgirokasse plans $500 mln 5-yr bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Landesgirokasse plans to launch a $500 million five-year international bond this week, bankers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The triple-A rated German bank has held roadshows for the transaction, which was expected to be aimed at European and Asian investors, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Landesgirokasse deal could be launched either today (Tuesday) or tomorrow,&quot; a syndicate manager at a European bank said.</p>
<p>Credit Suisse First Boston and Goldman Sachs were tipped as joint lead managers, but officials there were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Spread talk was around 11 basis points over U.S. Treasury notes, dealers said.</p>
<p>In the last year, Landesgirokasse has issued mark, Swiss franc, Luxembourg franc and French franc bonds.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
